<!-- cell: plot id="68dd0411-78f1-4cd8-9f16-b123a091cfdc" title="The custody of Captain Varn's daughter (high-level)" edges="07c6d506-62b0-4589-914e-4bd22e8854c5:46aad309-4217-4cd6-95af-7ef88d1c782c>b5e48725-08fd-44fa-82fc-4d2fb6cbad1e, 528f3fff-2a61-4df8-9859-2de94b90603c:b5e48725-08fd-44fa-82fc-4d2fb6cbad1e>12e6ea8d-915e-4453-b05f-caed071d16fd" -->

<ol title="How a lawyer fought to take Captain Varn's daughter from her, and lost the girl to the man Varn trusted.">
<li id="46aad309-4217-4cd6-95af-7ef88d1c782c" timestamp="2">Armed with the detective's evidence, Captain Varn's ex-husband hires a lawyer and sues for custody of their daughter while Varn is away on her mission to Mars.</li>
<li id="b5e48725-08fd-44fa-82fc-4d2fb6cbad1e" timestamp="3">At the hearings, Varn has to answer from her ship over a delayed link. The lawyer argues her dangerous assignment and her ties to a politician linked to the mafia, and the court leans toward the father.</li>
<li id="12e6ea8d-915e-4453-b05f-caed071d16fd" timestamp="4">Varn's ship is lost before the ruling. The politician asks for custody as Varn wished, the detective's evidence shows that the father only wanted to hurt her, and the court gives the girl to the politician.</li>
</ol>

<!-- cell: plot id="8f4f71f1-37ca-4d57-a0cf-45471d855f9a" title="The custody of Captain Varn's daughter (low-level)" edges="baea2afe-a380-488b-8a6c-fe480a595662:3de9da00-a114-44c2-b928-5a9a4607b20e>125e3aff-9837-4abf-b289-527ba3e949f5, 6707810e-3776-4402-b17f-f2d07b04a8c3:125e3aff-9837-4abf-b289-527ba3e949f5>cd62e9ff-c532-4813-89af-554fcbcab636, 750b8823-44dd-4838-901d-a782ca0568bc:cd62e9ff-c532-4813-89af-554fcbcab636>74048a74-1b5e-4b90-a21f-54044574db30, dfbe00c4-7b1b-4dcb-b8a0-d787076ab381:74048a74-1b5e-4b90-a21f-54044574db30>c58e4b7f-b365-4c69-9b62-1001dc2d6fc9, fac08b49-6ac7-4efa-aa6e-7fea5e450c82:c58e4b7f-b365-4c69-9b62-1001dc2d6fc9>e6e5cb18-ddf3-4bbb-a06f-af763b38d43b, 546955cd-360f-42f8-b501-205d64cb7154:e6e5cb18-ddf3-4bbb-a06f-af763b38d43b>dfe42004-939c-483e-9583-148504e78d3f, 1259a8c7-0369-4a37-9163-23d3ddcda356:dfe42004-939c-483e-9583-148504e78d3f>4a8327f1-a68b-4923-9884-de47f1b33e74, 93f1d7a7-bd76-466a-9d1b-c096ed1f94e3:4a8327f1-a68b-4923-9884-de47f1b33e74>145b23ba-cb74-4c19-bd9e-d9b934bc245f" -->

<ol title="Hired by Captain Varn's ex-husband, a lawyer sues for custody of their daughter while Varn is at Mars, turns the court against her with the detective's photographs, and, when Varn's ship is lost, sees the girl given to the politician once the father is shown to have only wanted revenge.">
<li id="3de9da00-a114-44c2-b928-5a9a4607b20e" timestamp="2.2" location="earth, the lawyer's office">Captain Varn's ex-husband brings a lawyer the detective's photographs, and hires her to win him custody of his daughter.</li>
<li id="125e3aff-9837-4abf-b289-527ba3e949f5" timestamp="2.3" location="earth, the court">The lawyer sues for custody: the mother is away on a dangerous mission, and keeps company with a man tied to the mafia.</li>
<li id="cd62e9ff-c532-4813-89af-554fcbcab636" timestamp="3.1" location="earth, the court">At the first hearing, Varn has to answer from her ship over a delayed link. Her answers arrive minutes late, and the court hears them as evasions.</li>
<li id="74048a74-1b5e-4b90-a21f-54044574db30" timestamp="3.2" location="earth, the court">The lawyer argues that Varn's assignment puts her life at risk, and leaves the girl with no parent at home.</li>
<li id="c58e4b7f-b365-4c69-9b62-1001dc2d6fc9" timestamp="3.4" location="earth, the court">She puts the detective's photographs before the court: Varn with the politician, and the politician at the doors of the company.</li>
<li id="e6e5cb18-ddf3-4bbb-a06f-af763b38d43b" timestamp="3.5" location="earth, the court">When news of the alien ships around Mars reaches the court, the judge leans toward the father: the girl needs a parent who will come home.</li>
<li id="dfe42004-939c-483e-9583-148504e78d3f" timestamp="4.1" location="earth, the court">The judge announces that she will rule for the father.</li>
<li id="4a8327f1-a68b-4923-9884-de47f1b33e74" timestamp="4.5" location="earth, the court">On the day of the ruling, word comes that Varn's ship is lost. The politician asks the court for custody of her daughter, as Varn asked him to.</li>
<li id="145b23ba-cb74-4c19-bd9e-d9b934bc245f" timestamp="5.1" location="earth, the court">The detective's evidence shows that the father only wanted to hurt Varn. The court gives the girl to the politician, and the lawyer is left knowing whom she fought for.</li>
</ol>
